.\" robodr-pulsard(8). Source of truth: the clap definitions in
.\" crates/robodr-pulsard/src/main.rs (Opts) and vendor/pulsar
.\" (PulsarDaemonOpts), plus clap-verbosity-flag. Keep in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-PULSARD 8 "2026-10-16" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-pulsard \- RoboDR: Pulsar runtime security agent with robot sensors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-pulsard
.RB [ \-\-config\-file
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-v ...]
.RB [ \-q ...]
.PP
.B robodr\-pulsard
.RB ( \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B robodr\-pulsard
is the Pulsar eBPF runtime\-security daemon with the RoboDR modules
registered (today the ROS 2 sensor,
.BR robodr\-sensor\-ros2 ).
Pulsar's process, file\-system and network probes and its rules engine run as
upstream; the RoboDR sensor watches ROS 2 discovery (SPDP socket and,
optionally, passive AF_PACKET capture) against the locked model profile.
.PP
RoboDR is protective only: it detects and reports. It never overrides the
robot's safety system, e\-stop or command authority.
.PP
It must run as root (Pulsar refuses otherwise). Under systemd the shipped
unit confines that root process with a capability bounding set and a
read\-only file system; see
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/robodr\-pulsard.service
and
.IR /usr/share/doc/robodr/PACKAGING.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-file " FILE"
Pulsar configuration file (TOML). Default
.IR /etc/pulsar/pulsar.toml ;
the shipped unit passes
.IR /etc/robodr/pulsar.toml .
RoboDR modules are off unless enabled in
.BI [module. name ]
sections. Unknown keys are only warned about.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase logging verbosity (repeatable). Default level: info.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Decrease logging verbosity (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the RoboDR version plus the Pulsar version and commit it embeds.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/pulsar.toml
Daemon configuration (dpkg conffile).
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/profile.json
Locked model profile (from
.BR robodr\-commission (1)).
Missing, unlocked or invalid: the sensor runs observe\-only.
.TP
.I /usr/share/robodr/rules/
Pulsar rules (RoboDR and upstream), read at module start.
.TP
.I /run/robodr\-pulsard/pulsar.sock
Pulsar API socket (as configured by the shipped
.IR pulsar.toml ).
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Linux 5.5 or newer with BPF and BTF
.RI ( /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux ),
and a bpf file system mounted at
.IR /sys/fs/bpf .
Live capture needs CAP_NET_RAW.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a clean shutdown, 1 on error (reported on stderr).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-commission (1),
.BR robodr\-ros2\-watch (1),
.BR systemd.exec (5),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
